	)
	(text "Two n8synth-style edge strips, 40 positions each at 2.54 mm. Each position is an outer hole (the deck's\nheader pin, Dn) joined to an inner hole (a wiring point, Wn) by the net DECK_Ln / DECK_Rn: one pin per hole.\nNothing else on the board connects to them: each module is wired by hand from the channel holes to the inner\nholes. Deck cells occupy positions 1-10, 16-25 and 31-40. The right strip serves only the 10HP deck: it has no\nholes at 11-15 and 26-30, and only the deck hole at 10, 16 and 31.\n10HP: the board sits parallel behind the deck and both strips are used. 6HP: the board sits at 90° and\nonly the left strip meets the deck's right-angle header."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.5 1.5))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9561d0d3-d9c0-54f8-b5e2-be94e2d2bb28")
	)
